            <div xml:id="d91-a6">

                <pb facs="0174" n="167" sameAs="frus:frus1894Nicaragua/pg167"/>

                <head>B.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <p>Rigoberto Cabezas, inspector-general of the Atlantic coast and general intendent
                    of the district of Siquia, considering:</p>
                <p>That the public peace has been disturbed in the city of Bluefields by an armed
                    rebellion.</p>
                <p>That it is the duty of the authority to resort to the best means for the
                    maintenance of order and security to society in use of the faculties with which
                    I am invested.</p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Decree.</hi></p>
                <list>
                    <item>First. Declaring the district of Siquia in a state of siege.</item>
                    <item>Second. The common offenses during the existence of martial law will be
                        judged by a military council. Given in Rama on the 12th day of the month of
                        July, 1894.</item>
                </list>
                <p>(Communicated.)</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">R. Cabezas.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
